{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/357863-demon-the-fallen-used-in-other-cwod-games","id":357863,"title":"Demon The Fallen used in other CWoD games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-02T16:14:39-08:00","id":357863,"title":"Demon The Fallen used in other CWoD games","content":"I've been wanting to ask some questions and bounce ideas about using DtF with other CoD games. When I run a game (I'm currently running a WtA game), I always use the whole WoD setting to represent the other supernatural elements. If the PCs run into a Mage, he is built and played using the MtA rules. Same goes with Vampires, Mummies, Wraiths, Hunters, Fae, etc. Most of the STs I have played with have done the same.<br /> <br /> What I am asking about is Demons and the Umbra. In the write up for DtF, it talks about how everything used to be one. that is all facets of reality were together. A flower was a flower, a smell, a song and a chemical process all at the same time. A separate realm was created by the Fallen for the souls of the dead to go to (the underworld/ lower Umbra). Then, when the Fallen were punished, the were cast in hell (the abyss?) which was a part of the lower Umbra. While the were imprisoned reality continued to splinter and the other layers of the Umbra came into being.<br /> In the rules for DtF it lists their abilities with the right Lore as being able to enter the Lower Umbra and deal with the dead. What I am assuming is that the reason for them to only be able to go to the Lower Umber is that was all there was when the were punished. Now that they have escaped and are back on earth, as they explore the world and how it has changed, would they eventually realize how much reality has fractured? An example could be the fact that if someone uses their true name anywhere the know it and have a chance of locating the person and even listen to what they are saying. If that person were in another layer of the Umbra, (say a Garou who has been fighting a Demon or its pawns and has somehow found out a name and is telling another Garou about it or asking some spirits about it) would the Demon be able to pinpoint the Garou and realize that there is another layer to reality. and from this could he then use his Lores to eventually enter the other layers of the Umbra. The same could go for a Mage some where doing a similar thing, and being found.<br /> <br /> The demons of DtF, used to be able to travel anywhere in creation before the fall. So would they then, as they relearn their abilities, again be able to do so? Would their Lores for entering the Lower Umbra be also usable to go to others parts of the Umbra as they learned about them? Or would they have to develop a new Lore to travel through the layers of reality as they are now?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts of ideas on this subject would be appreciated. Hopefully I made my self clear on my thoughts and questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:06:55-08:00","id":357980,"title":"","content":"Possibly because it was meant to mesh too well with Vampire, and Vampires can't access the Umbra that the Garou and Fera deal with - Auspex takes astrally projecting vampires to the Astral Umbra, and through a distinct path of necromancy, to the Dark Umbra. On the flipside, the metaplot shenanigans of D:TF alienated even further from potential and meaningful crossover possibilities, particularly with Werewolf, which didn't seem to ever acknowledge the existence of the Fallen at all. I mean, the Revised Storyteller's Handbook was written within a time frame where it could have included commentary on crossover with Demon, but it seems to have given it a giant and justifiable middle finger by omission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T22:35:23-08:00","id":358062,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">When I do Crossovers, I tweak each game a fair amount to help make them mesh (a process I call \u201cmythos-scaling\u201d).<br /> <br /> Crunch-wise, DtF and WtA need very little tweaking to work with one another (incidentally, I feel the exact opposite about the fluff).<br /> <br /> To your question: <br /> Yes, I totally think that Fallen learning about and gaining access into the Umbra (wolfy spirit-world-place) is totally doable. IIRC, it was the Slayers who could access the Underworld, but I think it would more appropriate for the Fiends (?-Angels of the Firmament?) to explore the spirit world of the Umbra. I don\u2019t think, however, Lore of the Spirit would be a good way to access the Umbra (unless you\u2019re taking the long way using some Yin-&gt;Yomi-&gt;Yang scenic route \u2013 and that\u2019s assuming you want to try throwing in some KOTE cosmology). <br /> <br /> If you\u2019re looking for some crunchy guidelines, maybe try meshing Lore of Paths and Lore of Spirit (The one from the Fiends and the one from the Slayers); something to open pathways into the \u201cother\u201d spirit world. <br /> <br /> These are my thoughts, but I\u2019m curious to see what more DtF-savvy players think. [Sounds like this would be right up Crowley\u2019s alley. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T01:12:28-08:00","id":358121,"title":"","content":"While most Rituals are utter crap in DtF, seriously a clearly combat application Ritual that takes 45 minutes to cast, this might be a good use for them. After all they do well enough job in how Bastions are made so they might be a suitable base for a mechanic to travel into the other Umbrae. Likely Requiring knowledge of both the Lore of Portals, or the Lore of Paths alternatively, and Lore of Spirits.<br /> <br /> The ritual would take some time but would open a portal, if using Lore of Portals, or a Pathway, if using Lore of Paths, that leads into the Umbra or back from there and allows for multiple passengers or infinite passengers for the time it remains open, depending on successes although I wouldn't keep them open for long for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> If using Devil's Due Demons just make it an Arcana with Open Gate and Spirit Sight as prerequisites and allowing one to open a Portal to any Spirit Realm, as Spirit Sight reveals all spirits, nature-, ghostly- and demonic-spirits equally and Open Gate is a rather powerful Arcana on it's own requiring it's own considerable prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}